ys out  beautifully worst the first act  struggles solos troubled production is  common knowledge at this point and the  first act of the film is supported that  seems to have been the most affected by  the film's production issues and  reshoots various tones and moments are  struggling for dominance which is to be  expected from a movie with multiple  directors nothing about the first 20  minutes of the film really works and  it's largely because it doesn't seem to  have any sense of where it stands  once Han Chewie and Beckett board  fastest ship solo finds itself but it  takes longer than it should to get there  best world building solo is that its  most engaging when it's building the  criminal underworld of star wars crimson  dawn a syndicate of mob bosses who run  the shady a corners of the galaxy is an  immediately intriguing concept ripe for  further exploration and the fact that  the Alpha is headed by Darth Maul is  even better on top of that solos  introduction of emphasis and a cloud  riders a gang of renegade refugees is a  fantastic piece of new Star Wars law  these bits of expansion come in small  pieces but as a whole former very  engaging look at corners of this galaxy  we've never seen before  worst over-explain the way solo builds  on star wars are great but it also goes  out of its way to explain details  perhaps best left to the imagination the  most prominent example is the Kessel run  in which harden the crew make the run  only narrowly avoiding death by a giant  tentacle creature is awesome but finding  out what the Kessel run is to begin with  still feel somewhat unnecessary  similarly certain aspects of Hans  origins are inevitable like how he and  Chewbacca come together but did we  really need to know how he came into  possession of a signature blaster the  abundance of explanation that nobody  asked for in solos serves little purpose  and ultimately shrinks some of the  possibilities in its massive universe  first bringing it home you ex